[h2]Build 0.9.119[/h2]
[h3]Changed[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Mending benches now sit the way vanilla workbenches do.[/b] The hand and electric benches were drawn squeezed inside their three tiles, so they looked a little small next to a tailor bench. The worktop now fills the three tiles and the legs show just below it, in every facing, and the tools on top are at vanilla scale.
[*][b]Lighter work scan when materials are short.[/b] Checking whether shelves, bookcases and other storage hold enough repair materials is now done once per scan instead of once per material per item, and the memo of "already tried, not enough" material lists no longer builds text for every item looked at.
[*][b]Idle repair centres do less.[/b] A repair centre with nothing on its item spot checks for new work less often after a few seconds, and picks the pace back up as soon as something arrives (at most a second and a half later). Its power check is cheaper too.
[/list]
[list]
[*]No gameplay changes. Safe to update mid-save.
[/list]
